            <ArticleTitle>An Unusual Cause of Rectal Stenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>406-409</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Solitary rectal ulcer syndrome (SRUS) is a benign disease that is often misdiagnosed. It is characterized by a combination of symptoms, endoscopic findings and histology. Patients present with constipation, rectal bleeding, mucous discharge, pain and a sensation of incomplete defecation. There are many different manifestations of this disease, with or without rectal prolapse. We report an unusual presentation of SRUS as a circular stenosis in a middle-aged male.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
